---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Install Veasel Code"
  description="Install Veasel Code on Linux, macOS, or Windows from GitHub Releases, Homebrew, or the AUR."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / INSTALL</p>
    <h1>
      Get a verified
      <br />
      <em>preview build.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Prefer an official archive with SHA-256 sums. Package managers track the
      same verified prereleases. No V compiler is required for the release
      binary.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Official archives</h2>
      <p>
        Download Linux, macOS, or Windows builds from the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/downloads/`}>downloads page</a> or{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/releases">
          GitHub Releases
        </a>
        . Each release publishes <code>SHA256SUMS</code>. Verify before you run.
      </p>
      <pre><code># After extracting the archive onto your PATH:
veasel --version
veasel</code></pre>
      <p>
        Archives include the V backend and a standalone <code>veasel-tui</code>.
        Bun is only needed when developing the terminal client from source.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Homebrew (macOS)</h2>
      <pre><code>brew tap veasel-labs/tap
brew install --cask veasel-code</code></pre>
      <p>
        Tap source:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/homebrew-tap">
          veasel-labs/homebrew-tap
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Arch Linux (AUR)</h2>
      <pre><code>yay -S veasel-code-bin</code></pre>
      <p>
        PKGBUILDs:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/aur-package">
          veasel-labs/aur-package
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>From source (contributors)</h2>
      <p>
        Use the V revision pinned in <code>.v-version</code>, SQLite headers for{" "}
        <code>db.sqlite</code>, and Bun 1.4.2+ for TUI development.
      </p>
      <pre><code>v run .
# or build, then:
veasel serve   # API only on 127.0.0.1:4097
veasel         # reuses or starts the server, then opens the TUI</code></pre>
      <p>
        See{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">
          CONTRIBUTING.md
        </a>{" "}
        and{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/RELEASES.md">
          docs/RELEASES.md
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Prereleases only.</strong> Verified pushes to <code>main</code>{" "}
      publish versioned previews. Checksums are part of the trust path — do not
      skip them for production-like environments.
    </aside>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/quickstart/`}>
        Next: first session <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/downloads/`}>
        Open downloads <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
